; `data`, `struct`, `type` and `effect` are template kinds; the rest
; are not, and the reserved prefix followed them into the type
; namespace. Four AX refusals, each at the place the reader can act on:
;
;   badMacro   a nested `macro` template - AX3021 at the MACRO's own
;              line, before any invocation exists, because a template
;              kind is a property of the macro. Refused by DECISION:
;              a macro generated in phase D would have to join the
;              macro table the same fixpoint is reading
;              (`trait` does not reach this refusal at all - it does
;              not parse in a template position, so it is AX2003 from
;              the parser, which is why the case here is a macro)
;   badImport  an `import` template - refused by DECISION rather than
;              by schedule: an import inside a template reopens
;              resolution ordering, which has already run when phase
;              D starts
;   the data   a `(syntax/join ...)` type name written OUTSIDE a
;              macro - AX3028, the same reservation a `fn` name gets,
;              now that a data name is parsed by the same function
;   the ctor   and the same for a constructor name
;
; The last two could not be written at all before this commit: the
; parser demanded a bare identifier in both positions, so the
; near-miss died as a syntax error naming the paren instead of the
; rule.
(macro badMacro ((badMacro T)
   (macro (inner x) x)))

(macro badImport ((badImport T)
   (import Str)))

(data (syntax/join Loose Ends)
  (Only))

(data Astray
  ((syntax/join Wander Off)))

(:: main Int)

(fn (main) 0)
